{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage","id":1522673,"title":"Do you think Mithras was involved in the war with Carthage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-16T10:45:32-07:00","id":1522673,"title":"Do you think Mithras was involved in the war with Carthage?","content":"I don't know if this was ever covered in the lore, but do you think everyone favorite Ventrue help spear head his clan's war with the Brujah ruled Carthage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T19:32:49-07:00","id":1522685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage#post1522673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this was ever covered in the lore, but do you think everyone favorite Ventrue help spear head his clan's war with the Brujah ruled Carthage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect Mithras only began to interest himself in Rome around the first century CE, so about two centuries after the destruction of Brujah power over Carthage, that is usually associated with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Punic_War\" target=\"_blank\">second punic war</a>, if memory tricks me not. I'd guess he was probably far more interested in playing with all the strife in the melange of empires and relgions rising and falling from the legacy of Alexander and the descendants of his generals, possibly alongside <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tiamat_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Tiamat</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Michael_(Toreador)\" target=\"_blank\">Michael</a> and other unmentioned ancients in a cabal of kindred infamous for their taste in playing deities.<br /> <br /> (I almost added Cybele to the package, but not only her story and identity are sketchy on many levels, but\u200b she claim <b>does </b>to have been involved in Carthage's fall - or one version of her supposedly did, it's complicated...)<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, i do believe the reason he disappeared from London during almost half the 19th century (exactly the time when british international influence reached its zenith) would be because he <i><b>was</b></i> personally spearheading the british conquest and colonization of the Indian subcontinent (in what diplomacy and obtaining support from local <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Danava\" target=\"_blank\">Danava</a> &quot;siblings&quot; played no small part) among other parts of the &quot;Far East&quot;. Definitely how i roll things in my games cryptolore, ocasional tall tales about this or that place where some group of local elders or a venerable ancient confronted him, with much destruction and masquerare-breaching displays involved. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-16-2023, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T22:55:50-07:00","id":1522686,"title":"","content":"If we go by actual history, Rome's war with Carthage were all during the era of the Republic while the Mithraic Mysteries did not arise until the Empire during the first through fourth centuries. So to me that indicates Mithras did not arrive in Rome until after the salting of Carthage during the Third Punic War (146 BC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T00:59:50-07:00","id":1522688,"title":"","content":"Carthage was planned to be the &quot;Third City&quot; the spiritual and political heir of the First and Second Cities and many of the Learned are like to think it that way<br /> Carthage's prince at the time was a coward and weakling named Himilcar the Pale (possibly, but not confirmed Child of Troile) - well at least his Clan blames him, because Clan documents indicate that he had trouble containing the Baali and the teachings of Tanitbaal-Sahar in his city, which resulted in even trusted agents turning against him, seeing the rituals of the Baali as better alternatives to preserving their city.<br /> The causes and effects are important here<br /> First, the Mortals of Rome and the Mortals of Carthage have their own differences and those - not surprisingly - allingned with the Vampire's interest and differences<br /> Namely the Ventrue of Rome became fierce rivals of the Brujah of Carthage.<br /> Not long after tales of a (degenerate) blood cults under Troile, human sacrifices \u2013 including infant sacrifices \u2013 to infernal powers rose up. And they had merits of course, since Moloch was a presence in the city from basically the begining<br /> You see, back in the ancient days Moloch and Nergal never really seen eye to eye, esepcially regarding Namtaru and it awakening. Nergal was an Infernalist, while Moloch was a Demonologist. Nergal was a follower and servant, while Moloch had a fairly pragmatic view on infernalism, seeking to use the demonic power without succumbing to it or bringing demons into the world.<br /> So in order to silence his brother and keep the bloodline from fracturing into a civil war - not to mention save the world he was lived in - he betrayed Nergal and his city Mashkan-Shapir to the Antediluvians, who reacted just as he anticipated. While the Baali War raged he took his most loyal childer and follwoers with him and left for the colony of Qart-\u1e25ada\u0161t, which would later be known as Carthage.<br /> Trolie her/himself was not a stranger to the darker things starting with the Diablerie, but the Baali remember Nergal was the one most adept at dealing with other Cainites. It is said that he served as Arikel's wench, debated philosophy with Troile and traded vice secrets with the Tzimisce Antediluvian, just to name a few.<br /> So when Troile and Moloch met, he had some ground to work on so to speak already<br /> Moloch became a confidant to Troile, knowing of his dark hunger and encouraging this aspect in him. Soon, Baali became one of the most influential vampiric lines within the city, demanding blood sacrifices and worship from the mortal inhabitants. Under Moloch's influence, Troile became much more moody, draining his enemies of their vitae and Embracing childer just to devour them. In time, the two became lovers, unknown to the rest of Moloch's brood.<br /> But something strange happened... Moloch and Troile became truly lovers - and that secret got out. It was a weakness in the eyes of many Baali, especially the Baali Elder Cybele, who was the Child of Nergal (or at least re-embraced by him)<br /> When the Second Baali War ended with the eruption of Mount Thera, <b>Cybele </b>was one of the few Baali to escape and her hatred against Moloch and his progeny was bottomless. 1,400 years later Cybele reappeared and disguised her bloodline so she could support the Roman Ventrue's war of annihilation against Carthage.<br /> So, as Moloch drew Troile into desensitization and degeneration, news of the endemic corruption among Carthaginian Brujah spread to the Roman clans.<br /> The Malkavian seeress <b>Tryphosa</b> gave guidance to the Roman prince <b>Camilla (Titus Venturus Camillus) </b>directing him to act against Carthage, and the Carthaginian Toreador <b>Helena</b> betrayed her city to the Romans. Through the Toreador Antediluvian, Artemis Orthia, Lysander and prince Alchias an alliance formed against the Brujah of Carthage; under the leadership of the Roman Ventrue the alliance encompassed the Malkavians, Toreador, Lasombra and their allies.<br /> It was Cybele's ritual that forever bound Toriel and Moloch beneath the ashes and salted earth of Carthage after they sunk in the earth embracing each other at the final battle as the Third Punic War razed Carthage in 146 BC.<br /> Drakonskyr, a Demon in the body of Lanta/Tiamat also looked for ways to cause widespread destruction by manipulating various nations to war: Babylonia, Persia, Greece, Rome, and many more so technically Demons and Infernalist were involved on both sides with a health dose of mortal greed and desire to rule the area and Rome and Carthage ulitmatelly went against each other becasue of the clashing political ,economical and territorial influence<br /> <br /> The Cult of Mithras quickly spread in the Orient and when Mithras heard of Rome, he chose to travel there. The Roman armies fascinated him, as he had been a soldier himself in life, and he accompanied them to the various corners of the Empire, preferring it to the stale Cainite politics in Rome itself. His cult spread through the military and became one of the great mystery religions in the Imperium Romanum by the time of the Roman Emperors. Mithras himself settled in Londinium in 71 CE<br /> So Mithras was in or around Rome with a quite an influence in the Army at least on the spiritual level and coming from the &quot;east&quot; - he was born in the territory where Iran is now located, and served in the military as a general of one of Indo-Iranic tribes. - was quite familiar of the Baali threat and demonic influence (especially if you consider that area was a very close neighbor of the Kuei-Jin and the Yama Kings) - even tho' he was &quot;only&quot; Embraced in 1258 BC, after the First and Second Baali Wars, so he not seen the their full might, but even after their defeat, their influence and effects are lingered and Mithras was one of the few who was in speaking terms with Haqim whos clan suffered greatly and fougth ever since with the Baal (again rumors say that Cybele appeared one last time a thousand years later after Carthage, at the Iblii-al-Akbar organ pit in Chorazin, to help Annazir and other Baali curse the Assamites with a terrible blood thirst)<br /> <br /> So technically Mithras was there that time and had every reason to be involved the War, but we don't have any canon material that would mention his name regarding the War<br /> But he Storyteller have enough freedom to use him as a participant or at least his cult's influence in the army even if himself not stepped a battlefild (but since Mithras was always a Soldier first then a relegious icon, it is highly possible he tore off a few heads)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 09-17-2023, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T03:58:23-07:00","id":1522697,"title":"","content":"Why would he side with Rome? The Romans to him, would have been nothing more than swamp-dwelling, Eastern-step speaking barbarians. And if you looked at it from his perspective, with the Arabian-Peninsula being the center of the world, Europe and Carthage, would have been considered, &quot;Colonies&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T10:44:34-07:00","id":1522711,"title":"","content":"The same could be said of why he went to England when it largely ruled by Celtic tribes and he loves being a soldier and was eager to test his skills and prove his claims being a God. If I remember from Fall of London, our Ventrue didn\u2019t feel a strong loyalty to his Persia roots. I bet in his early nights he was in a number of battles outside of Persia and had nothing to do with his homeland. And it also sounds like he hasn\u2019t made many trips back to the place he was born and embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-17-2023, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T16:16:24-07:00","id":1522805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage?p=1522711#post1522711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same could be said of why he went to England when it largely ruled by Celtic tribes and he loves being a soldier and was eager to test his skills and prove his claims being a God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to point out that Mithras moving to the British Isles was possibly around the time Christianity rose to power in the Roman Empire, but not only someone in the wiki seems to disagree and would claim he settled around 71CE. More importantly, i can find no clear statement of a time in his original write-up from A World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That said, the same original write-up does mention him and his companions setting themselves up as deities &quot;in a growing city westward, between two great rivers&quot; - what sounds very much like a reference to Mesopotamia, imho - and how he would abandon his companions about the time the romans began to leave a mark in the region, what for me implies the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_VI_Eupator#Mithridatic_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Mithridatic Wars</a>, and the anexation of the Seleucid Dynasty domain, from 89-63BC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage?p=1522711#post1522711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember from Fall of London, our Ventrue didn\u2019t feel a strong loyalty to his Persia roots. I bet in his early nights he was in a number of battles outside of Persia and had nothing to do with his homeland. And it also sounds like he hasn\u2019t made many trips back to the place he was born and embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, to be fair, being of persian origin doesn't play much of a role in his identity as a character. But being a vampire <i>playing god to his mystery cult</i> most certainly does, what makes trying to insert him in Punic Wars era Roman Republic sketchy, based on what is known of the spread of mithraism from Central Asia to the west and makes the core of most posters arguments <b>against</b> such an idea.<br /> <br /> All of that said, Mithras' own backstory mentions that his role as a sun god started as a prank of sorts in his worshippers - meaning he already was worshipped as deity with a cult-herd <b>before</b> that, implying that either Mithras changed divine roles/portfolio through the centuries (of what <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo\" target=\"_blank\">Apollo</a>, who started as prophetic and plague/healing god, only to later expand into a god of arts and the sun, makes a very visible historical example).<br /> <br /> Or Mithras is the last, <b><i>but not the only god</i></b>, the ancient Ventrue has used as a mask of sorts across the ages. Make of that what you will and play with the angle that seems more entertaining to one's chronicle - tweaking the lore for fun, story hooks and profit is very much part of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, loving to reread the British Isles background from a World of Darkness for the considerable number of gems of forgotten lore peppered into it, like the black plague developing <i>a variant that would affect even kindred</i>, mostly from 10th or thinner generations and how Mithras' suspicion of a Tremere-Setite alliance part behind this unnatural plague would spark a series of witch hunts and the centuries of Ventrue-Tremere conflict under his rule and that of his sucessors. Or how the London Brujah apparently played a major role in supporting Henry's VIII's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acts_of_Supremacy\" target=\"_blank\">Acts of Supremacy</a>, as part of a campaign to shake the Ventrue mortal power base and influence, among other curious or outright bizarre bits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T17:30:52-07:00","id":1522809,"title":"","content":"If you want to fudge the timeline a little bit, it was Mithras' support in Carthage that helped his Cult to take root and begin growing in Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T04:31:53-07:00","id":1522820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage?p=1522809#post1522809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to fudge the timeline a little bit, it was Mithras' support in Carthage that helped his Cult to take root and begin growing in Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Transylvanian Chronicles already gives us a very straight example of fudging of the dates with the PCs being sent to found the Siebenb\u00fcrgen in the 1190s, possibly 1-3 centuries before it actually happened in the real world, so there's precedent for a group to install Mithras in Rome a 1-2 centuries before Mithraism historically arrived in the Adriatic's shores.<br /> <br /> Plus, as i pointed out in my previous post, the ancient Ventrue's cult has not always been the same, the sun worship becoming a part of his mysteries after cult was already a thing, as a prank of sorts, according to his own backstory, what opens room of either a different older version of his cult - or the possibility that &quot;Mithras&quot; is just one name among several the ancient Ventrue has used across the millenia.<br /> <br /> <br /> What bringing Mithras into the Punic Wars narrative and vice-versa - or any other canon methuselah of one's preference, be it Menele, Helena, Critias, Beshter, Tiamat, Dracon, Montano, Antonius the Gaul, Cybele, Zarathustra, Ankla Hotep or whoever - adds to one's own chronicle seems like a more interesting matter to adress, at least imho.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-20-2023, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T10:54:58-07:00","id":1522836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522673-do-you-think-mithras-was-involved-in-the-war-with-carthage?p=1522688#post1522688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carthage was planned to be the &quot;Third City&quot; the spiritual and political heir of the First and Second Cities</div> </div> </div> </div>Gratuitous random aside but, in my own most recent chronicle, the &quot;Third City&quot; is also a popular/infamous kindred moniker, specially among certain anarch, sabbat and fringe circles for the city of Berlin after the &quot;False Caine&quot; crisis of the early 90's, when the visitation of a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ankla_Hotep\" target=\"_blank\">so called Caine</a> and birth of his impromptu personality cult toppled the already fractured local power structure. A major mess that took about one year for the Camarilla to solve - and the fact this resolution came through a &quot;negotiated armistice&quot; with the cultists and their own de-mobilization in nomadic coteries &amp; packs spreading all across Europe &amp; beyond as &quot;Caine&quot; left in mysterious affairs of his own, instead of an actual takeover/victory has left something of a bitter taste in the halls of the Ivory Tower for decades.<br /> <br /> That alongside with supposed Caine sightings during the &quot;Ankaran Sarcophagus debacle&quot; in L.A. has made for some tumultuous relations between the sects and the budding presence of the &quot;Witnesses of Caine&quot;, specially with their &quot;pilgrims&quot; following on rumoured steps of the First of the Kindred in my latest chronicle.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-25-2025, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reacti